  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased capacity of constituents for  enhanced productivity and decent work in the agricultural and textile supply chains</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The private sector is key for Syrian socio-economic recovery and is a sustainable entry point for humanitarian assistance in Syria to build resilience and alleviate people&#x2019;s suffering in a protracted crisis. ILO will support private businesses in selected productive sectors with job creation potentials, namely the textile and agri-food industries, along their supply chains. 
At the institutional level, ILO will support its social partner, namely the Damascus Chamber of Industry, in its efforts to review its strategy and the establishment of a renewed action plan.</narrative>
  </description>
